---
import '../styles/global.css';
---
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>XEMA Engine | Andueza Dev</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="container">
      <a href="/" class="back-link" style="display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 2rem; color: var(--accent-color); text-decoration: none;">← Back to home</a>
      
      <h1>XEMA: Custom 3D Engine</h1>
      <p style="font-size: 1.2rem; color: #94a3b8;">A high-performance C++ engine built from scratch. Designed for cross-platform scalability, mastering memory management, math, and rendering pipelines.</p>

      <section class="tech-section" style="margin-top: 3rem; border-top: 1px solid #334155; padding-top: 2rem;">
        <h2>Technical Architecture</h2>
        <div class="feature-list" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem; margin-top: 1rem;">
          <div class="feature-item" style="background: #1e293b; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px;">
            <h3>Core Systems</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Job System:</strong> Thread pool using std::future for asynchronous model loading and procedural generation.</li>
              <li><strong>ECS:</strong> Data-oriented design with O(1) component access and ID-based entity management.</li>
              <li><strong>Scene Graph:</strong> Hierarchy system integrated directly into component arrays.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-item" style="background: #1e293b; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px;">
            <h3>Graphics & HAL</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Modern OpenGL:</strong> 4.5+ DSA (Direct State Access) pipeline.</li>
              <li><strong>Rendering Techniques:</strong> Deferred Shading, Shadow Mapping (PCF), and PBR (Metallic/Roughness).</li>
              <li><strong>Platform Abstraction:</strong> Zero-overhead HAL resolved at link-time without virtual dispatch.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-item" style="background: #1e293b; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px;">
            <h3>Platform Porting</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Nintendo Switch:</strong> Ported via libnx and EGL, supporting both Docked (1080p) and Handheld (720p) modes.</li>
              <li><strong>Build System:</strong> Integrated devkitPro Makefile with Premake5 for single-codebase management.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="tech-section" style="margin-top: 3rem; border-top: 1px solid #334155; padding-top: 2rem;">
        <h2>Development Experience</h2>
        <p>This project focused on solving low-level challenges, such as implementing a custom Physics Manager (PhysX 5), script integration via Lua/sol2, and asynchronous I/O to ensure the main loop never stalls.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>